 "prompt_sent": "Recorded: the digital edition stays on the system it runs on today, reviewed when the £500k test is read (Decided). That puts the review at about the end of September 2028, a year after the last print issue (my reading), so the current system has to carry the move and the first year.\n\nHard to reverse: every option, because an announcement can't be taken back, including A, which looks simplest.\n\n[Q14 · 7 of 8 settled] In what order do you tell staff, advertisers and subscribers?\n\n- **A.** All three on the same day (the minimum).\n- **B.** Staff first, then advertisers, then subscribers, each on its own date (the most flexibility).\n- **C.** Staff first, then advertisers and subscribers together on one later date (the easiest for the common case).\n\nMy recommendation: B, because staff would otherwise hear it from advertisers or subscribers, and advertisers need time with their digital offer before the public announcement."
